%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b31be19987964df6b8d40557c558639f, type: 3}
  m_Name: OnboardingResources
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Features.Tutorial.Onboarding.Data.OnboardingResources
  explainerTexts:
    _serializedList:
    - Key: 0
      Value: Welcome, Merchant! This is a game about trade.\nYou will help the local
        towns develop by delivering what they need... and make a pretty coin along
        the way.
    - Key: 1
      Value: In this introduction, you will develop Town A and Town B to tier II.
        Towns grow by consuming the goods you sell them, through trade missions and
        in various other ways.
    - Key: 2
      Value: "It looks like Town B has an active trade mission for hay right now.
        You\u2019re currently in Town A, which happens to produce hay. Buy 15, travel
        to Town B and sell them the hay."
    - Key: 3
      Value: Well done! Fulfilling mission gives you a cash reward and raises the
        towns development and growth.
    - Key: 4
      Value: In the meantime, Town A got ready to be upgraded. To upgrade them to
        Tier II, you need to fulfill their upgrade mission. You can see all ongoing
        missions by pressing [F2] or using the overlay button in the bottom of the
        screen.
    - Key: 5
      Value: Town A needs berries to progress to tier II. Town B does not have berries
        yet, but they are available in the neighboring forest. Towns can only build
        producers for the resources in neighboring regions. Build a berry picker
        in Town B.
    - Key: 6
      Value: Nicely done! Production buildings not only produces goods, but also
        bump up the towns development and reputation of you!
    - Key: 7
      Value: "It will take some time to amass the 30 berries needed for Town A\u2019s
        upgrade mission. You can wait here and let some days pass by unpausing the
        game via\_[Space]. To further speed up time, press\_[2]."
    - Key: 8
      Value: There are now enough berries. Deliver them to Town A to complete their
        upgrade. While you're at it, you should also buy some game. The more goods
        a town has bought, the faster they develop. And the more goods you get to
        sell, the higher your margins!
    - Key: 9
      Value: To fit more than one good into your caravan, you must first upgrade
        your cart to the next level. Upgrading your caravan makes it faster and adds
        more storage space. But beware the increasing upkeep costs for larger caravans.
    - Key: 10
      Value: Good job! Town A has been upgraded to Tier II. It has improved production
        speed and earns more coin, which is great news for you, as they can buy more
        goods off of you at once. Upgrading a town also unlocks the next tier of
        goods, which have much better earning potential for you.
    - Key: 11
      Value: "With everything you\u2019ve learned, go ahead and help Town B get to
        tier II. Town A has some untapped resources in the neighboring fields that
        will surely come in handy. "
    - Key: 12
      Value: One final tip, before I let you find your fortune on your own. Medieval
        Merchant is all about trading favorably. To understand whether a deal is
        amazing or the worst trade deal in the history of trade deals, make sure
        to hover the price in the trade menu with your mouse. It will give you a
        detailed overview of all the factors that impacted the prices of this good
        at this specific moment.  Good luck out there!
